A random bot never opens a trade on its own.
Touches: modules/mod-playerbots/src/Ai/Base/Actions/TradeAction.cpp,
TradeAction::Execute()

Why: reports #92/#93 -- "playerbots keep initiating trade" / "don't allow
the bots to start trades, they are spamming it all dungeon long".

The RPG behaviour set includes RpgTradeUsefulAction ("give an item this
nearby player could use better"), whose trigger only requires a player
within line of sight, some friendship roll, and a useful item in the bot's
bags. It routes through TradeAction, which resolves a target from the chat
text or falls back to the master -- but a random bot has no master, so any
real player nearby became a trade target, repeatedly, for the whole run.

The gate sits at the initiate site rather than in the RPG trigger so every
other path into TradeAction is covered too. A trade may still be *completed*
with whoever opened it: this only refuses CMSG_INITIATE_TRADE, and only for
random bots without a real-player master. A bot invited to its master's
group trades exactly as before.

--- a/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Ai/Base/Actions/TradeAction.cpp
+++ b/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Ai/Base/Actions/TradeAction.cpp
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include "ChatHelper.h"
 #include "Event.h"
 #include "ItemCountValue.h"
 #include "ItemVisitors.h"
 #include "PlayerbotAI.h"
+#include "RandomPlayerbotMgr.h"

 bool TradeAction::Execute(Event event)
 {
@@ -34,6 +35,14 @@
             player = botAI->GetMaster();

         if (!player)
+            return false;
+
+        // A random bot never opens a trade on its own. Reports #92/#93: bots
+        // were spamming trade requests at real players all dungeon long, from
+        // the RPG "trade useful" behaviour picking a nearby player as target.
+        // A trade may still be *completed* with whoever opened it -- this only
+        // gates CMSG_INITIATE_TRADE, and only for bots nobody invited.
+        if (sRandomPlayerbotMgr.IsRandomBot(bot) && !botAI->HasRealPlayerMaster())
             return false;

         if (!player->GetTrader())
